From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maxim Stepanov <g.maxim.stepanoff@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 11:05:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent: make LLM completion retry policy configurable

The agent's retry policy for failed LLM completions was hardcoded to 4
attempts with a 5s base delay. Providers that enforce a low
requests-per-minute limit frequently exhaust those four retries before
the limit window clears, so the turn fails. This is especially painful
for subagents, which fan out concurrently and hit the shared RPM budget
hard.

Expose an `agent.retry` settings block controlling the maximum number of
attempts (with `0` meaning unlimited), the base delay, and a cap on the
exponential-backoff delay. The policy applies only to rate-limit and
server-overloaded errors; every other retryable error keeps its fixed
internal cap so genuine failures still surface. Subagents are `Thread`
instances sharing the same retry path, so they inherit the policy with
no extra wiring.

The run-loop attempt counter is widened to `u32` to support unlimited
retries, and the retry-status UI omits the "of N" denominator when the
policy is unlimited.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
